 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Archetypes from retrieved Wikipedia pages: Mac Pro, Alienware Aurora, HP Z, iMac, Mac mini, Mac Studio, Dell OptiPlex, Intel NUC, HPE ProLiant MicroServer, Dell PowerEdge. Tower list cut from 74 to 7 models: Dell Precision SKU run trimmed to current models; DECpc, Compaq ProSignia and Epson Endeavor MR7300 dropped as dated SKU noise. Low-profile desktop renamed Small-form-factor desktop: Amiga 1000/1500/2000/2500/3000/4000 and Atari Mega/Mega STE/TT030 go to the Vintage computers shelf (Vintage desktop computer); DECpc LP/LPv/LPx runs dropped. Rack-mount server renamed Home server and cut to two lines with a few homelab-relevant models; enterprise SKU runs (PowerEdge R6xx/R7xx, ThinkSystem, Supermicro) dropped by the scope rule. Tower and AIO models remain Dell-heavy because the old data was a Dell harvest and no new models were researched. MicroServer generation list not given on the retrieved page, so only N36L (named there) is listed; Mac Pro \"cheese grater\" nickname not on the page, so not used."
}